# sisukas #89 — SISU Kori API: study-event identity and locations
#
# For VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client) or another .http-compatible client.
# Fill in the IDs below using actual Aalto SISU records.
# Run requests in order: realisation -> study event -> location -> building.
# Some documented Kori endpoints may be unavailable or require authorization
# on Aalto's installation. Keep 401/403/404 responses as investigation results.
#
# Reference schema: https://sisu.helsinki.fi/kori/docs/index.html
# No authentication header is provided intentionally: this probes public access.

@baseUrl = https://sisu.aalto.fi/kori/api
@realisationId = aalto-cur-P-c235941a-0fd6-11f1-8c99-0050569455c9
@studyEventId = aalto-SE-ASIO-9000815-7339722
@anotherStudyEventId = aalto-SE-ASIO-9000816-7339890
@locationId = aalto-TILA-457
@alternateLocationId = aalto-TILA-488
@buildingId = aalto-RAKENNUS-R037

### 1. Course-unit realisation — inspect studyGroupSets, subgroups and studyEventIds
# Documented Kori v1 endpoint.
GET {{baseUrl}}/course-unit-realisations/v1/{{realisationId}}
Accept: application/json

### 2. Course-unit realisation — verified unversioned endpoint
# Returns the same realisation data as the versioned endpoint
# for the investigated course.
GET {{baseUrl}}/course-unit-realisations/{{realisationId}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Study events — verified unversioned batch endpoint
# Returns an array of study-event records, including expanded occurrences.
# The investigated record matches the versioned endpoint.
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events?id={{studyEventId}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Study event — documented versioned endpoint
# Inspect id, locationIds, events, recurring rules, exceptions,
# cancellations, and per-occurrence overrides.
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events/v1/{{studyEventId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Another study event — contrast ordinary class vs exam/exception
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events/v1/{{anotherStudyEventId}}
Accept: application/json

### 6a. Study events — verified batch lookup with repeated IDs
# Confirmed on Aalto SISU: returns an array containing both records.
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events?id={{studyEventId}}&id={{anotherStudyEventId}}
Accept: application/json

### 6b. Study events — comma-separated batch lookup
# Verified on 2026-10-27: returns both requested study-event records.
# This is the format currently used by SisuClient.fetch_study_events().
# Both comma-separated and repeated id parameters work for the tested IDs.
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events?id={{studyEventId}},{{anotherStudyEventId}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Location — room and building information
# Inspect id, localized name, capacity, buildingId, and embedded building.
# Verified example: TU1 Saab Auditorium - 1017, Maarintie 8.
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations/v1/{{locationId}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Alternate location — exam room
# Verified example: AS2 - 2006, Maarintie 8.
# This is a different series-level location, not an irregularLocationIds
# override. Occurrence-level relocation remains to be investigated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations/v1/{{alternateLocationId}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Building — optional standalone lookup
# Use buildingId from request 7 or 8.
# Location responses may already embed building names and addresses.
GET {{baseUrl}}/buildings/v1/{{buildingId}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Location export — restricted discovery endpoint (optional)
# Returned 401 Unauthorized without credentials on 2026-10-27.
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations/v1/export?since=0&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 11. Building export — restricted discovery endpoint (optional)
# Returned 401 Unauthorized without credentials on 2026-10-27.
GET {{baseUrl}}/buildings/v1/export?since=0&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 12. Study-event export — restricted discovery endpoint (optional)
# Returned 401 Unauthorized without credentials on 2026-10-27.
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events/v1/export?since=0&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### Verify the current wrapper's comma-separated ID format
GET {{baseUrl}}/study-events?id={{studyEventId}},{{anotherStudyEventId}}
Accept: application/json